    "description": "Application architect and software developer on the life safety product development team. Provided full-stack web application and mobile application development since product inception for the Quantum Safety and Security system (Named on US Patent 10,186,095). Developed Android mobile alerting and system management application. Developed and managed CI/CD (Jenkins) pipelines. Lead initiative to containerize application. Authored Ansible Playbooks for configuration management.\n\nResponsible for system architecture and deployment of JNL's cloud application strategy on AWS. Designed a scalable, highly available back-end architecture for an emergency mass notification solution. Refactored an internal legacy monolith application to a distributed architecture, leveraging both traditional and serverless solutions.\n\nDeveloped health screening application (JNL SafeHealth) from concept to product release. Provided full-stack development (Web App, Android Kiosk App, Python/Flask REST API, and CI/CD) for application.\n\nDeveloped dashboards (CloudWatch and Grafana) to provide both technical and business insights.\n\nProvided engineering support to the technical support team. Developed scripts, SQL queries, and tools for assisting support team and end users in automating system deployments. Assisted with training technical support team members.\n\nAdministrated Atlassian suite for engineering team (Jira, Confluence, Bitbucket). \n\nCo-wrote end user and installer documentation for JNL product lines.",
